* mv_package — MVPKG helper: where is this version's SOURCE artifact?
* Copyright (C) 2026 Gordon Heydon.  GPL-2.0-only (see LICENSE).
*
* MVPKG.SRCURL(NAME, VER, REG, SURL) — SURL = the tarball URL of package NAME's
* SOURCE artifact at version VER (VER="" for the current one), or "" when the
* registry does not serve one.  Relative, as the registry publishes it, unless
* the asset is externally hosted — the caller joins it to REG the same way it
* does for META<3>.
*
* A SEPARATE QUESTION FROM MVPKG.META, which is why it is a separate program
* rather than a flag on that one.  MVPKG.META asks "what should this machine
* install?" and sends the platform in the query so the registry can answer with
* a prebuilt binary.  This asks "where is the source?", which has nothing to do
* with this machine -- so it sends NO platform, and selectArtifact then leaves
* the tarball at the package's own, which for a version that published a source
* asset IS that asset.
*
* AND IT CHECKS WHAT CAME BACK.  With no platform the registry reports
* `selected: source` whether or not a source artifact exists: a binary-only
* package's `tarball` is its first BINARY asset (indexRelease), reported as
* source because nothing was selected.  So the caller must already know a
* source artifact is published -- META<13>, which SRCINC reads -- and this
* refuses to return a URL that came back under any other selection.
*
* HTTP/JSON/MAPFIELD are MVX intrinsics; the other ports reach them as the
* cataloged seam functions, so the bootstrap wrappers are declared here for the
* same reason MVPKG.META declares them (#133): installing the first package is
* this client's job, so it cannot depend on a package being installed already.
* FLAT GUARDS, one per platform -- an $IFDEF nested inside an $ELSE compiles on
* UniData and fails on UniVerse.
   SUBROUTINE MVPKG.SRCURL(NAME, VER, REG, SURL)
   $INCLUDE MVPKG.INC PLATFORM.H
$IFDEF JBASE
   DEFFUN HTTPGET(A)
   DEFFUN JSONDECODE(A, B)
   DEFFUN MAPFIELD(A, B, C, D, E)
$ENDIF
$IFDEF UDT
   DEFFUN HTTPGET(A) CALLING "*MVPKG.HTTPGET"
   DEFFUN JSONDECODE(A, B) CALLING "*MVPKG.JSONDECODE"
   DEFFUN MAPFIELD(A, B, C, D, E) CALLING "*MVPKG.MAPFIELD"
$ENDIF
$IFDEF UV
   DEFFUN HTTPGET(A) CALLING "MVPKG.HTTPGET"
   DEFFUN JSONDECODE(A, B) CALLING "MVPKG.JSONDECODE"
   DEFFUN MAPFIELD(A, B, C, D, E) CALLING "MVPKG.MAPFIELD"
$ENDIF
   SURL = ""
   IF TRIM(NAME) = "" THEN RETURN
   SPEC = ""
   SPEC<-1> = MAPFIELD("name", 1, "", "", "")
   SPEC<-1> = MAPFIELD("tarball", 2, "", "", "")
   SPEC<-1> = MAPFIELD("selected", 3, "", "", "")
   Q = ""
   IF TRIM(VER) # "" THEN Q = "?version=" : TRIM(VER)
   BODY = HTTPGET(REG : "/package/" : NAME : Q)
   IF BODY = "" THEN RETURN
   SM = JSONDECODE(BODY, SPEC)
   IF SM<1> = "" THEN RETURN
   IF TRIM(SM<3>) # "source" THEN RETURN
   SURL = TRIM(SM<2>)
   RETURN
